+### 0412 — Symbol reachability is not semantic coverage, and 48 bindings measured 2/394
+
+- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/traceability` proved two things about a `section_binding` — the named Go declaration parses and exists, and the linked acceptance case is registered with an executable test. Neither compares the implementation against the section it claims, so a sliver satisfied a whole-section binding and `tracecheck -section X` reported it as owned. `section:2.2` (22 unconditional lease/replica invariants) was bound to `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which validates one enum and a name grammar; `section:18.4` (audit retention) was bound to `OpenProjection`, and no retention code exists. Three independently produced branches reached that state without anyone noticing.
+- FINDING: the consequence is not a wrong report, it is a licence to do nothing. Any future Story assigned §2.2 or §18.4 would have found the section already owned and could legitimately have closed with no work.
+- FIX: every `section_binding` declares a `coverage` level and the gate recomputes it. Denominator measured from `internal/specdoc` — RFC 2119 clause lines under the heading *and its subheadings*, so a parent is measured over its children. Numerator = the clauses the binding enumerates, each of which must index that inventory, declare its exact `SPEC.md` line, quote it verbatim beginning on that line, and name an acceptance case the binding itself owns. Declared level must equal the measured bucket. Assigned-scope admission now requires `full`; repository-wide verification stays green on an honest registry.
+- EVIDENCE: 48 bindings discharge **2 of 394** normative clauses. full=1, sliver=1, unevidenced=43, unmeasured=3, unowned=2. Assigned-scope admission succeeds only for §6.2. (Revision 1 also admitted §7.3, §13.14.5 and §15.2 on the false ground that their pinned sections carry no obligation of their own; see the entry below.)
+- FINDING: `MAY`/`SHOULD` are excluded from the denominator deliberately. Counting them would inflate the ratio and make coverage look worse than it is, which is the same dishonesty in the other direction.
+- ANOMALY: no shipped binding could honestly be declared `full` except §6.2, whose single clause is "terminal backend MUST be `conpty`" on native Windows — already discharged by `TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` through the production `Load`. Without it the positive arm of the gate could only have been proven synthetically. A gate whose admit path is never exercised on shipped data is not much better than one that is always green.
+- FINDING: the disclosure surfaced two more of the same shape that no audit had named. `section:17.2`'s single clause is an unknown-event *reader* obligation while its binding names the Configuration *writer* `EncodeCurrent`; `section:2.1`'s single clause is a replica runtime obligation nothing here implements. §6.5 kept its binding but its gap names a real defect: SPEC.md:2585 requires `required_capabilities` to default to the platform lane minimum, and `internal/config/validation.go:670` accepts only an empty default.
